{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 37","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rob is helping to build the set for a school play. For one scene, he needs to build a multi-colored tetrahedron out of cloth and bamboo. He begins by fitting three lengths of bamboo together, such that they meet at the same point, and each pair of bamboo rods meet at a right angle. Three more lengths of bamboo are then cut to connect the other ends of the first three rods. Rob then cuts out four triangular pieces of fabric: a blue piece, a red piece, a green piece, and a yellow piece. These triangular pieces of fabric just fill in the triangular spaces between the bamboo, making up the four faces of the tetrahedron. The areas in square feet of the red, yellow, and green pieces are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5aba31be6646779e396ad0a1d05095132c3a2bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. If the blue piece is the largest of the four sides, find the number of square feet in its area. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc522a6043ee11eb362c256925a4139fc16f1cc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import three; unitsize(1cm); size(200); draw((0,0,0)--(0,0,10)); draw((0,0,0)--(0,30,0)); draw((0,0,0)--(40,0,0)); draw((40,0,0)--(0,30,0)--(0,0,10)--(40,0,0),dotted); label(&quot;a&quot;,(0,10,0),S); label(&quot;b&quot;,(15,0,0),S); label(&quot;c&quot;,(0,0,5),E);  currentprojection=orthographic(1,1/2,1/2);  [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"178\" />\n</p><p>Let the three lengths of the rods be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.  Since the hypotenuse of the three right triangles are longer than the legs of the right triangle, the blue piece uses the lengths of the hypotenuses.  For the red, yellow, and green pieces, right triangles are used, so write three equations based on the area.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/32705fccdb289b329e4cfff968c3505338d7c960.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab = 120\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc072d929b9af6a87295fe4f6f30b3089e44055.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[bc = 40\\]\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a240f1ad94eff1b04117555885b9262216be1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ac = 30\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />\nSolving this equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c353286712355599ce3b6ec1d547ae5064c23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c371f51eefa141ff561c4b7e5fd8dc5028239048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 4\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1561185866347d81d746e495bb6c9f76d7a592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, the three side lengths of the blue piece are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21cab8170b74a93aa634b9b075b87c55cd176b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b94b1d1d325c7a6fe8147538b29d99ede6f5bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{170}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e3d5cf7e29a189c48d71d5cbf6c7f040c0be585.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import three; unitsize(1cm); size(200); draw((0,0,0)--(0,0,10)); draw((0,0,0)--(0,30,0)); draw((0,0,0)--(40,0,0)); draw((40,0,0)--(0,30,0)--(0,0,10)--(40,0,0),dotted); draw((0,0,0)--(96/5,72/5,0)--(0,0,10),dotted); label(&quot;$5\\sqrt{10}$&quot;,(20,15,0),SE); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{170}$&quot;,(15,0,5),NW); label(&quot;10&quot;,(0,20,5),NE);  currentprojection=orthographic(1,1/2,1/2);  [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"178\" />\n</p><p>Draw the altitude of the triangle with lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bc0d2ed4f5e05a87c193c2c1e39d9e4fc48c5b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e120fbc5a5b6c5d47db236d02ea85893696c6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />.  Because the area of the red piece (one with lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bc0d2ed4f5e05a87c193c2c1e39d9e4fc48c5b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e120fbc5a5b6c5d47db236d02ea85893696c6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the length of the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4a805e10744671db719f589d0ebbc6c5f5c9a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12\\sqrt{10}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" />.  The hypotenuse of the triangle with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4a805e10744671db719f589d0ebbc6c5f5c9a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12\\sqrt{10}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b621a121050f645e5f3815b39bf3eca7cb0f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13\\sqrt{10}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" /> and is perpendicular to the side with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21cab8170b74a93aa634b9b075b87c55cd176b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> (since it is on the same plane as the altitude), so the area of the blue piece is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a58e5f9c9d331799ee0329f7731c87902492c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{13\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\cdot 5\\sqrt{10}}{2} = \\boxed{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"155\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 36\">Problem 36</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 38\">Problem 38</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Proble